# Version Control Rules -- Swaroop Formulation Industries

## Progressive Branching Strategy

### Levels 1-2 (Beginner / Elementary)
- Two branches: `main` (stable) and `dev` (active development).
- Direct commits to `dev`, merge to `main` for releases.
- Manual git tags on `main` after each milestone.

### Levels 3-4 (Intermediate / Upper Intermediate)
- GitFlow model:
  - `main` -- production-ready code.
  - `develop` -- integration branch.
  - `feature/<name>` -- new features (branch from `develop`).
  - `release/<version>` -- release preparation.
  - `hotfix/<name>` -- urgent fixes (branch from `main`).
- All merges via Pull Requests with at least one review.
- Conventional Commits enforced.

### Levels 5-6 (Advanced / Expert)
- Trunk-based development with feature flags.
- Short-lived feature branches (max 2 days).
- Protected `main` branch with required CI checks.
- Signed commits required.
- Automated changelog generation from conventional commits.

## Tag Convention

Format: `v{MAJOR}.{MINOR}.{PATCH}-{level-descriptor}`

| Tag | Level | Milestone |
|---|---|---|
| `v0.1.0-l1-chatbot-basic` | 1 | Foundation chatbot deployed |
| `v0.2.0-l2-rag-enabled` | 2 | RAG pipeline with vector search |
| `v0.3.0-l3-agentic-rag` | 3 | Agentic RAG + certifications page |
| `v0.4.0-l4-adaptive-dashboards` | 4 | Adaptive RAG + dashboards + ETL |
| `v0.5.0-l5-full-platform` | 5 | Full platform with GenAI automation |
| `v1.0.0-l6-production` | 6 | Enterprise production release |

## Pull Request Template

```markdown
## Summary
<!-- 1-3 bullet points describing what this PR does -->

## Level
<!-- Which roadmap level does this belong to? L1-L6 -->

## Type of Change
- [ ] feat: New feature
- [ ] fix: Bug fix
- [ ] docs: Documentation
- [ ] refactor: Code restructuring
- [ ] test: Tests
- [ ] ci: CI/CD
- [ ] chore: Maintenance

## Checklist
- [ ] Code follows project conventions (.cursor/rules/project_conventions.mdc)
- [ ] Documentation updated in both .md and .tex formats
- [ ] Prompt log updated if AI was used
- [ ] Environment variables added to .env.example
- [ ] No secrets committed
- [ ] Tests pass locally
```

